  "backgrounds": [
    {
      "id": 110,
      "name": "Endpoint",
      "script": "-- The REST client every card shares. The Connection card holds the\n-- settings: the base URL, the headers to send (such as an Authorization\n-- token) and a timeout. Each card shows the request it made, the status\n-- and the raw JSON that came back.\n\nfunction apiGet path\n  put card field \"Base URL\" of card \"Connection\" into base\n  set the httpHeaders to card field \"Headers\" of card \"Connection\"\n  get card field \"Timeout\" of card \"Connection\"\n  if it is a number then set the httpTimeout to it\n  put base & path into theURL\n  put \"GET\" && theURL into field \"Request\"\n  put url theURL into reply\n  put the result into problem -- empty when it worked\n  if problem is empty then put \"OK\" into field \"Status\"\n  else put problem into field \"Status\"\n  put reply into field \"Response\"\n  if problem is not empty then return empty\n  return reply\nend apiGet\n",
